    </li>
                </div>
                            </div>
                    
                </div>
        </div>
        
    </div>



<h2 class="wp-block-heading">FAQ </h2>


<div class="wp-block wp-block-faq" id="accordion-6b023c64d0a10" >
                    <div class="wp-block-faq__item" >
                                    <div role="button" tabindex="0" aria-expanded="false"  data-hc-collapse-trigger="accordion-6b023c64d0a10-0" aria-controls="accordion-6b023c64d0a10-0" >
                        <h3 class="wp-block-faq__item__title iris-appearance__title"
                            >
                            Why is Nice called Nice?
                            <i class="ficore ficore--chevron-bottom" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                            </h3>
                    </div>
                                                    <div class="collapse "
                                                 data-hc-collapse="accordion-6b023c64d0a10-0" id="accordion-6b023c64d0a10-0"
                         data-hc-collapse-parent="#accordion-6b023c64d0a10" >
                        <div class="wp-block-faq__item__content iris-appearance__content" >
                            <p class="isSelectedEnd">There are two main hypotheses regarding the origin of the name Nice:</p>
<p class="isSelectedEnd">The first dates back to the 4th century BC, when the Phocaeans, a people from Greece, sought to expand their presence after founding Massalia (Marseille). They settled in what is now known as the Old Town of Nice and founded Nikaia (also spelled Nikéa or Nikê). In Greek, this name means &#8220;victory.&#8221;</p>
<p>Historian Luc Thévenon, however, believes that the name Nice may have Ligurian origins. In that language, it means &#8220;a spring&#8221; or &#8220;a fountain,&#8221; referring to the waters of the sea.</p>

                        </div>
                    </div>
                            </div>
                    <div class="wp-block-faq__item" >
                                    <div role="button" tabindex="0" aria-expanded="false"  data-hc-collapse-trigger="accordion-6b023c64d0a10-1" aria-controls="accordion-6b023c64d0a10-1" >
                        <h3 class="wp-block-faq__item__title iris-appearance__title"
                            >
                            When did the city of Nice become French?
                            <i class="ficore ficore--chevron-bottom" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                            </h3>
                    </div>
                                                    <div class="collapse "
                                                 data-hc-collapse="accordion-6b023c64d0a10-1" id="accordion-6b023c64d0a10-1"
                         data-hc-collapse-parent="#accordion-6b023c64d0a10" >
                        <div class="wp-block-faq__item__content iris-appearance__content" >
                            <p>Nice officially became part of France in 1860, following the annexation of the County of Nice under the Treaty of Turin on 24 March 1860, confirmed by a popular vote held on 15 and 16 April 1860.</p>

                        </div>
                    </div>
                            </div>
                    <div class="wp-block-faq__item" >
                                    <div role="button" tabindex="0" aria-expanded="false"  data-hc-collapse-trigger="accordion-6b023c64d0a10-2" aria-controls="accordion-6b023c64d0a10-2" >
                        <h3 class="wp-block-faq__item__title iris-appearance__title"
                            >
                            What can I do in Nice in 3 days?
                            <i class="ficore ficore--chevron-bottom" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                            </h3>
                    </div>
                                                    <div class="collapse "
                                                 data-hc-collapse="accordion-6b023c64d0a10-2" id="accordion-6b023c64d0a10-2"
                         data-hc-collapse-parent="#accordion-6b023c64d0a10" >
                        <div class="wp-block-faq__item__content iris-appearance__content" >
                            <p>In three days in Nice, you can explore the Cours Saleya, visit the Matisse Museum, join the guided tour &#8220;When Nice Invented the Riviera,&#8221; and taste local specialities such as socca and pan bagnat. <a href="https://www.explorenicecotedazur.com/en/explore/towns-villages/coastal-area/nice/what-to-do-in-nice/">Discover our suggestions here</a>.</p>

                        </div>
                    </div>
                            </div>
                    <div class="wp-block-faq__item" >
                                    <div role="button" tabindex="0" aria-expanded="false"  data-hc-collapse-trigger="accordion-6b023c64d0a10-3" aria-controls="accordion-6b023c64d0a10-3" >
                        <h3 class="wp-block-faq__item__title iris-appearance__title"
                            >
                            What can I see and do in Old Nice?
                            <i class="ficore ficore--chevron-bottom" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                            </h3>
                    </div>
                                                    <div class="collapse "
                                                 data-hc-collapse="accordion-6b023c64d0a10-3" id="accordion-6b023c64d0a10-3"
                         data-hc-collapse-parent="#accordion-6b023c64d0a10" >
                        <div class="wp-block-faq__item__content iris-appearance__content" >
                            <p>During your visit to Old Nice, we recommend exploring the Cours Saleya Flower Market, discovering Place Rossetti and its fountain, or joining a guided tour of Old Nice offered by the Nice Heritage Centre.</p>

                        </div>
                    </div>
                            </div>
                    <div class="wp-block-faq__item" >
                                    <div role="button" tabindex="0" aria-expanded="false"  data-hc-collapse-trigger="accordion-6b023c64d0a10-4" aria-controls="accordion-6b023c64d0a10-4" >
                        <h3 class="wp-block-faq__item__title iris-appearance__title"
                            >
                            Where can I swim in Nice?
                            <i class="ficore ficore--chevron-bottom" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                            </h3>
                    </div>
                                                    <div class="collapse "
                                                 data-hc-collapse="accordion-6b023c64d0a10-4" id="accordion-6b023c64d0a10-4"
                         data-hc-collapse-parent="#accordion-6b023c64d0a10" >
                        <div class="wp-block-faq__item__content iris-appearance__content" >
                            <p class="isSelectedEnd">You can swim at the beaches along the Promenade des Anglais or at La Réserve.</p>
<p class="isSelectedEnd">On the Promenade des Anglais, Lenval Beach is open to dogs.</p>
<p>You will also find many private beaches offering sunbed rentals, restaurants and other services.</p>

                        </div>
                    </div>
                            </div>
                    <div class="wp-block-faq__item" >
                                    <div role="button" tabindex="0" aria-expanded="false"  data-hc-collapse-trigger="accordion-6b023c64d0a10-5" aria-controls="accordion-6b023c64d0a10-5" >
                        <h3 class="wp-block-faq__item__title iris-appearance__title"
                            >
                            How do I get to Castle Hill in Nice?
                            <i class="ficore ficore--chevron-bottom" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                            </h3>
                    </div>
                                                    <div class="collapse "
                                                 data-hc-collapse="accordion-6b023c64d0a10-5" id="accordion-6b023c64d0a10-5"
                         data-hc-collapse-parent="#accordion-6b023c64d0a10" >
                        <div class="wp-block-faq__item__content iris-appearance__content" >
                            <p>You can reach Castle Hill on foot via the Lesage stairs, the streets of Old Nice, or from the port via Rue Ségurane. There is also a free lift located near Rue des Ponchettes.</p>

                        </div>
                    </div>
                            </div>
                    <div class="wp-block-faq__item" >
                                    <div role="button" tabindex="0" aria-expanded="false"  data-hc-collapse-trigger="accordion-6b023c64d0a10-6" aria-controls="accordion-6b023c64d0a10-6" >
                        <h3 class="wp-block-faq__item__title iris-appearance__title"
                            >
                            Are there any casinos in Nice, France?
                            <i class="ficore ficore--chevron-bottom" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                            </h3>
                    </div>
                                                    <div class="collapse "
                                                 data-hc-collapse="accordion-6b023c64d0a10-6" id="accordion-6b023c64d0a10-6"
                         data-hc-collapse-parent="#accordion-6b023c64d0a10" >
                        <div class="wp-block-faq__item__content iris-appearance__content" >
                            <p class="PDq2pG_selectionAnchorContainer" data-start="18" data-end="251">Yes, there are two casinos in Nice: Casino Barrière Le Ruhl, located at 1 Promenade des Anglais, and Casino Partouche at the Palais de la Méditerranée, located at 15 Promenade des Anglais.</p>

                        </div>
                    </div>
                            </div>
                    <div class="wp-block-faq__item" >
                                    <div role="button" tabindex="0" aria-expanded="false"  data-hc-collapse-trigger="accordion-6b023c64d0a10-7" aria-controls="accordion-6b023c64d0a10-7" >
                        <h3 class="wp-block-faq__item__title iris-appearance__title"
                            >
                            Where is Nice-Saint-Augustin train station located?
                            <i class="ficore ficore--chevron-bottom" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                            </h3>
                    </div>
                                                    <div class="collapse "
                                                 data-hc-collapse="accordion-6b023c64d0a10-7" id="accordion-6b023c64d0a10-7"
                         data-hc-collapse-parent="#accordion-6b023c64d0a10" >
                        <div class="wp-block-faq__item__content iris-appearance__content" >
                            <p>Nice-Saint-Augustin train station is located in the Arenas district, in the western part of Nice, in the immediate vicinity of Nice Côte d’Azur Airport.</p>

                        </div>
                    </div>
                            </div>
            </div>
    
    
